TO ADD FILTERING TO THE ACTUAL ITEM BLOCKS SEE THE ITEM CONTAINER RIGHT BELOW THIS FILTERING TAGS BAR TO LINK THESE FILTER TAGS WITH YOUR ITEMS

Title your Main category between <h1> and </h1>

Under the Catergory title, there's the main button group codes, you can name these after the catergories or simply number them, they group the filter tags so if you click "all" on a different catergory, it doesn't completely reset the entire page

For the main tag (eg "All") the default code is:

<button class="button is-checked" data-filter="">

the "is-checked" is the intitial checked box. For all other sub tags use this code for EACH new filter

<button title="Filter Name" class="button" data-filter=".filter"><b>ICON HERE</b></button>

Change the filter name to what your filter is called, change the .filter to the filter link you want, ie location, type of location, hiring or not, etc. 

All icons are from here: 
https://remixicon.com/

Simply search for an icon, click on the desired icon and copy the icon code and paste where noted on the filter code

For example here are some filter tags I'd need

<button title="houses" class="button" data-filter=".houses"><b><i class="ri-community-line"></i></b></button><button title="Wanted" class="button" data-filter=".wanted"><b><i class="ri-information-2-line"></i></b></button><button title="Female" class="button" data-filter=".female"><b><i class="ri-user-6-line"></i></b></button>

